# The line numbers are in the editor's own area, not under the explorer. A gutter of
# three digits starts at x = 224, puts a number two cells in, right-aligned, so the "1"
# of the first line, the current one and so in the text colour, is at 224 + 32 = 256:
# 29 pixels in Unscii. The "2" below it, in the dim colour (32 pixels), is at the same x
# and is not at x = 32 in the explorer, which has nothing on that row.
# files t.txt=x\ny
# open t.txt
# frames 4
# pixels 256 0 264 22 223 225 230 29
# pixels 256 22 264 44 137 147 160 32
# pixels 32 22 40 44 137 147 160 none
1 key b ctrl
